os8088 patch 07: the PicoMEM, as its own firmware.

A new ISA memory-card device, `isamem0_type = picomem`, that is a thin
adapter around libpmhost - the PicoMEM's firmware compiled for the host by
os8088's tools/picomem/build.sh and loaded at run time with dlopen, so this
patch builds with no dependency on it. Every I/O and memory cycle the card
decodes goes to the firmware; its decode is mirrored into 86Box per 8-port
block and per 8 KB block, so nothing else on the bus changes; card time is
the machine's, in 100 us ticks, and its DAC is mixed in at 48 kHz.
Config: [PicoMEM #1] irq, sd_image, lib, usb_mouse (86Box's pointer as the
card's USB mouse, polled every 8 ms; the machine's own mouse must be
none), and for a 2.x library irq3/irq5/irq6/irq7 (its jumpers: each pin
reaches its line only when set) and dma (its DRQ channel, 1 or 3): the
2.x's real DMA is a DRQ the card raises per byte, answered from 86Box's
8237 with dma_channel_read after each card slice. The card's NE2000 (a Pico W's Wi-Fi
bridge) reaches 86Box's network through a companion NIC, net_01_card =
picomem_ne2k, which network.c starts like any card.
tools/os88box.py resolves lib and copies sd_image like a disk.

docs/plans/completed/PICOMEM-EMU-PLAN.md section 5.1.

